# A floor or mod of a multiple of the divisor plus one term c·v, c a
# divisor of it, and a constant below c reads the multiple divided and
# the floor or mod of the rest: the row indices of census kernels
# 01588.ptx and 00203.ptx, a mod of four times a warp index plus 1, and
# an alignment, each store's address with its sectors per warp request.
# With p bound to 0, ⌊(16·p·%tid.x + 1)/16⌋ reads p·%tid.x, so its
# product with %tid.y, 0, is refused and the address is unknown.
RUN: %ptxroof analyze %fixtures/micro/floor_mod_remainder.ptx --bind 1:p=0 | FileCheck --check-prefix=ANN "%s"
ANN: {{^}}	st.global.u32 	[%rd3], %r1; // global store [4·⌊(%tid.x mod 128)/16⌋ + param_0 + 32] sectors/req 1 (ideal 1){{$}}
ANN: {{^}}	st.global.u32 	[%rd3], %r1; // global store [128·%ctaid.y + 4·⌊(%tid.x mod 64)/2⌋ + param_0] sectors/req 2 (ideal 2){{$}}
ANN: {{^}}	st.global.u32 	[%rd3], %r1; // global store [16·(⌊%tid.x/32⌋ mod 4) + param_0 + 4] sectors/req 1 (ideal 1){{$}}
ANN: {{^}}	st.global.u32 	[%rd3], %r1; // global store [256·%ctaid.y + 64·⌊(%tid.x mod 64)/16⌋ + param_0] sectors/req 2 (ideal 1){{$}}
ANN: {{^}}	st.global.u32 	[%rd3], %r1; // global store addr ? (depends on special register %tid.x, in a product){{$}}
